Small fixes to realesrgan-ncnn-vulkan; the command line and its messages stay
as upstream has them.

- Windows: format the model paths with %ls/%d. Upstream passes a std::string
  through swprintf's "...", which is undefined and only happened to work.
- Other systems: snprintf instead of sprintf into the 256-byte model path
  buffers, which a long -m path overflowed.
- Stop with exit status -1 when the .param or .bin file can't be opened or
  parsed (ncnn or the Windows branch has already said why on stderr), instead
  of running an empty network. On Windows, upstream went on to read from a
  null FILE*.
- Windows: check and create the output folder as a wide path; path::string()
  throws for characters outside the ANSI code page.

